    "Html": "<p>NutritionFacts.org arises from my annual review of the medical literature. With the help of a team of hundreds of volunteers, we churned through tens of thousands of papers published in the peer-reviewed scientific nutrition literature and are ramping up to break new records in 2020. How do I choose which studies to highlight? In general, I strive to focus on the most groundbreaking, interesting, and useful findings; but which topics resonate the most? The practical ones, offering cooking or shopping tips? Or those that dissect the studies behind the headlines? Maybe it’s the geeky science ones exploring the wonderfully weird world of human biology? As you can see from the below list, the answer seems to be a bit of all of the above:</p>\n<h5><strong>#10 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/time-restricted-eating-put-to-the-test/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Time-Restricted Eating Put to the Test</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18.jpeg/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-60899 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"Time-Restricted Eating Put to the Test\" width=\"205\" height=\"115\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/48-18.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 205px) 100vw, 205px\"/></a>I was so excited to start to put all my intermittent fasting videos up. This one was more of a backgrounder. The thrilling conclusion can be found in <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-benefits-of-early-time-restricted-eating/\">The Benefits of Early Time-Restricted Eating</a>, a video that ended up changing my own family’s eating habits.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#9 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/eggs-and-breast-cancer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Eggs &amp; Breast Cancer</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer.jpeg/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-56044 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"eggs and breast cancer\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-14-Eggs-and-Breast-Cancer.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>How few eggs should we eat to reduce the risk of prostate, ovarian, colon, and breast cancer?  This was part two of a three-part video series. The others were <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dietary-cholesterol-and-cancer/\">Dietary Cholesterol &amp; Cancer</a> and <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/oxidized-cholesterol-27HC-may-explain-3-breast-cancer-mysteries/\">Oxidized Cholesterol 27HC May Explain 3 Breast Cancer Mysteries</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#8 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-it-best-to-drink-tap-filtered-or-bottled-water/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Is It Best to Drink Tap, Filtered, or Bottled Water?</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-59593 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Is It Best to Drink Tap, Filtered, or Bottled Water?\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/47-16-Is-It-Best-to-Drink-Tap-Filtered-or-Bottled-Water_.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>When I was writing the hydration chapter in <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How Not to Diet</a></em> I figured I should do a deep dive into the best water filtration system. Given the disinfection byproducts in tap water, Brita, PUR, ZeroWater, and refrigerator water filters are put to the test. </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#7 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-butter-really-back-what-the-science-says/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Is Butter Really Back? What the Science Says</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-56075 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"Is Butter Really Back? What the Science Says\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/01/45-18-Is-Butter-Really-Back_-What-the-Science-Says.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>Years ago I tried to put the controversy to rest with my videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-saturated-fat-studies-set-up-to-fail/\">The Saturated Fat Studies: Set Up to Fail</a> and <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-saturated-fat-studies-buttering-up-the-public/\">The Saturated Fat Studies: Buttering Up the Public</a> but it keeps rearing it’s buttery head.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#6 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/kidney-stones-and-spinach-chard-and-beet-greens-dont-eat-too-much/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kidney Stones and Spinach, Chard, and Beet Greens: Don’t Eat Too Much</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-59138 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"Kidney Stones and Spinach, Chard, and Beet Greens Don’t Eat Too Much\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/47-02-Kidney-Stones-and-Spinach-Chard-and-Beet-Greens-Don’t-Eat-Too-Much.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>Given their oxalate content, how much is too much spinach, chard, beet greens, chaga mushroom powder, almonds, cashews, star fruit, and instant tea? Wait, what are oxalates? You may want to also check out the prequel video <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/Oxalates-in-Spinach-and-Kidney-Stones-Should-We-Be-Concerned/\">Oxalates in Spinach and Kidney Stones: Should We Be Concerned?</a></p>\n<h5><strong>#5 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-diabetes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Best Diet for Diabetes</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-57774 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"The Best Diet for Diabetes\" width=\"199\" height=\"112\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/46-7-The-Best-Diet-for-Diabetes.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 199px) 100vw, 199px\"/></a>The case for using a plant-based diet to reduce the burden of diabetes has never been stronger and the good news is that finally the guidelines are starting to catch up: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/plant-based-diets-recognized-by-diabetes-associations/\">Plant-Based Diets Recognized by Diabetes Associations</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#4 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/which-is-a-better-breakfast-cereal-or-oatmeal/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Which Is a Better Breakfast: Cereal or Oatmeal?</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-58611 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"Which Is a Better Breakfast, Cereal or Oatmeal?\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/05/46-18.-Which-Is-a-Better-Breakfast-Cereal-or-Oatmeal_.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>One of the things I learned while writing <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How Not to Diet</a> </em>was the importance of not just whole grains but <em>intact</em> whole grains, the remarkable impact of the structure of food beyond nutritional content or composition.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#3 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-cook-greens/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to Cook Greens</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-58875 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"How to Cook Greens\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/06/46-26-How-to-Cook-Greens.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>Dark green leafy vegetables are the most nutrient-dense foods on the planet. What’s the best way to prepare them? What about other vegetables? Another popular video this year was <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-way-to-cook-vegetables/\">Best Way to Cook Vegetables</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#2 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/keto-diet-theory-put-to-the-test/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Keto Diet Theory Put to the Test</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-61899 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1-1024x536.png\" alt=\"Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1\" width=\"202\" height=\"106\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1-1024x536.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1-960x502.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1-768x402.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1-720x377.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Keto-Diet-Theory-Put-to-the-Test-1-540x283.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 202px) 100vw, 202px\"/></a>Multiple videos from my ketogenic diet series made the top 10, but I decided to just list one, but you can find the rest <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/keto-diet/\">here</a>!</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h5><strong>#1 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Evidence-Based Weight Loss</a></strong></h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-60989 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-1024x576.png\" alt=\"Evidence Based Weight Loss\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B-540x304.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/11/EBWL-Thumbnail-Option-B.png 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>Even though this just came out recently it’s already skyrocketed to the single most watched video of the year. It offers a sneak peek into <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>How Not to Diet</em></a>. If you want to watch the one I did on my last book check out <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/books/\">How Not to Die</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-61897\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1-1024x540.png\" alt=\"Obesity webinar\" width=\"476\" height=\"251\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1-1024x540.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1-960x506.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1-768x405.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1-1200x633.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1-720x380.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1-540x285.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/12/Obesity-Wide-1.png 1210w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 476px) 100vw, 476px\"/></a></p>\n<p>In 2019 I did a series of webinars on fasting, which you can find <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-bundle-digital\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-bundle-digital\">here</a>. They were so popular I decided to do a whole series of webinars on a variety of topics in 2020 (in between my 200-city <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/pages/speaking-dates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/pages/speaking-dates\">speaking tour</a>!). The first one explores the origin of the obesity epidemic. Obesity exploded throughout the industrialized world in the late 1970s. What happened? Any potential driver would have had to be global in nature and coincide with the upswing of the epidemic. So how do the various explanations stack up?</p>\n<p>I hope you’ll join me as I sift through all competing theories and answer your questions in this 2-hour live webinar. Check out the full list of topics <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinar/obesity-epidemic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\n<p>To join, make a donation with <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=44&amp;&amp;test=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">this form</a> ($20 is the suggested amount) and we will send you a link to register for the webinar as a donor reward. Your support helps NutritionFacts.org undergo its own explosion in global growth!</p>\n<p><strong>Webinar Date &amp; Time: </strong>January 24, 2020, 2pm ET<br/>\n<strong>Last Day to Register:</strong> January 16, 2020</p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><u><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><u><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><u><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><u><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><u><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></u></a></li>\n</ul>"
  }
